# Generic build-context ignore — applies to ALL images and, crucially, to the LEGACY docker
# builder too. Per-Dockerfile ignore files (e.g. Dockerfile.sandbox.dockerignore) are a BuildKit
# ONLY feature; a legacy build silently ignores them and `COPY . /app` then bakes secrets + the
# answer key into the image. This file makes the isolation boundary builder-independent. Keep it a
# superset of the security-critical entries in Dockerfile.sandbox.dockerignore.
.git
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
spikes
spec/references
# Secrets — must never enter any image (#137, trusted-submitter creds never reach a worker).
.env
# Isolation (#137): the agent runs inside the sandbox image — no datasets (the ablation answer key
# lives under data/*/verifier/), no prior run results, no analysis figures.
data
results
figures
